when im dead and the worms and bugs eat my brain, theyll see you

theyll see you how i saw you, hear the way you said my name. as they feast on the edges of my brain, theyll taste all the memories of us, every bite will bring them closer to a fragment of you; every moment will be steeped in the desire, the passion and even the sorrow and remorse i felt

but in time, your memory will fade, my body will wither, and the bugs will continue, because that is the only fate they were ever meant to follow
